<title>USA: First Western to merge units, cut costs.</title>
<headline>First Western to merge units, cut costs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW CASTLE, Pa. 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Western Bancorp Inc said on Thursday that it plans to merge its thrift and trust subsidiaries into its largest subsidiary, First Western Bank, to cut costs.</p>
<p>In a statement, First Western said the merger would not affect customers, but would reduce regulatory and administrative expenses.</p>
<p>In a separate transaction, the bank said, First Western Trust Services Co will be merged into First Western Bank, and become the bank's trust department.</p>
<p>First Western Bancorp said the consolidation would not cause any lay-offs.</p>
</text>
